From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: StellarSeal <emnoigi1452@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 17:02:11 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 092/204] Defer light checks until neighbor chunks are loaded

World.c discards a light check when the 3x3 chunk neighborhood of the changed block is not fully loaded (island and region edges); nothing recomputes it, so the light stays wrong. With defer-light-updates (default true) the check is remembered per chunk (PendingLightRegistry, chunk-local packed ints, capped) and replayed in recording order, budgeted per tick, once the neighborhood is complete (hooked after Chunk.loadNearby links neighbors; cleared on unload; drained before the chunk map flush). Checks whose own chunk is not loaded are still dropped, as before.

Config (optimizations.lighting): defer-light-updates (true), deferred-light-updates-per-tick (1024; 4096 measured ~35-60 ms in a dense light-emitting case), deferred-light-max-entries (262144). Deliberate deviation from vanilla: strictly more light is computed, never less.

Finding recorded in DeferredLightUpdateTest: vanilla's incremental relight is path dependent. Placing sources and relighting after each gives a different result than placing all first and relighting afterwards (1147 differing block-light cells for three torches), because the second source's search finds its cell already raised and the radius-17 limit is measured from the first source. Replay therefore equals running the same checks after all of the block changes. This is likely the mechanism behind broken lighting after bulk pastes and motivates the async bulk relight step.

Tests: PendingLightRegistryTest (pack/unpack, cap, budget carry-over, WAIT/GONE, clear, visitor re-entrancy), DeferredLightUpdateTest (replay equals running the same checks after all changes, per-tick budget, toggle off keeps vanilla, unloaded center not recorded, out-of-range Y), DeferredLightPerfTest: normal fully loaded path 27.6 ms vs 25.7 ms with the toggle (noise, branch not taken); recording 4096 checks 2 ms; replaying one default budget (1024 checks) 9.2 ms. Not covered: a real chunk load/unload sequence on a running server.

